<title>UK: Hanson up as Laing rates long-term &quot;buy&quot;.</title>
<headline>Hanson up as Laing rates long-term &quot;buy&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Hanson Plc were firm on Wednesday as analysts at Credit Lyonnais Laing issued a long-term &quot;buy&quot; recommendation on the stock, dealers said.</p>
<p>Hanson shares were up 3p at 302-1/2 by 1100 GMT, after rising as high as 307 -- equalling its highest level since the spin-off of its Energy Group Plc unit, the final stage in a demerger programme begun in 1995.</p>
<p>Analysts at Laing were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
</text>
